# Shell commands and target environments

## Shell commands (RTK) — required

**Always** prefix agent shell commands with **`rtk`** when RTK supports the underlying tool (~60–90% token savings on pytest, git, ruff). Passthrough is safe if no filter exists.

Two layers (use both on native Windows):

1. **Global hook** — `rtk init --global --agent cursor` adds `preToolUse` to `~/.cursor/hooks.json` (see `docs/ai_assisted_development.md`).
2. **Explicit prefix** — agents still write `rtk uv run …`, `rtk git …` in every command (required on Windows; recommended everywhere).

| Use RTK for | Example |
| ----------- | ------- |
| Git | `rtk git status`, `rtk git diff -- <paths>`, `rtk git log -5` |
| Tests | `rtk uv run pytest <path> -q` |
| Lint / format | `rtk uv run ruff check ./src ./tests` |
| Docker | `rtk docker compose ps`, `rtk docker compose logs --tail=20` |
| Postgres | `rtk psql …` |
| Diffs / find | `rtk diff …`, `rtk find …` |
| Large file reads | prefer the `Read` tool; shell fallback: `rtk read <file>` |

Install (Windows): extract `rtk-x86_64-pc-windows-msvc.zip` to `%USERPROFILE%\.local\bin` and add to PATH. Verify: `rtk --version`, `rtk gain`. Do **not** use `pip install rtk` (wrong package).

## Target environment approval

**Always ask** before running any command that is not read-only.

**Safe without asking** (local only):

- `rtk uv run pytest`, `rtk uv run ruff`
- `uv sync`
- `rtk git diff`, `rtk git status`, `rtk git log`
- Local `alembic` against the local dev database
- Local `rtk uv run uvicorn` for development (port 8001)

**Requires approval**:

- Live API calls with real keys (`WeatherAPITask` hits OpenWeatherMap)
- `git push`, network `git pull`
- Any deploy or production-side command

**When blocked or awaiting approval**: show the exact command for copy-paste; do not run it.

Override RTK for one command: `RTK_DISABLED=1 uv run pytest …`
